%T A123444 8242518
%N A123444 Number of partner-graph triangle-free perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123444 Two vertices x and y of a graph are partners if there are vertices u, v, w, distinct from x and y, such that {x,u,v,w} and {y,u,v,w} each induce a path P_4. The partner graph has the same vertex set and joins partners. A graph is counted if it is perfect and its partner graph is triangle-free. The class is closed under induced subgraphs. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Oct 10 2026
%H A123444 S. Hougardy, <a href="http://www.or.uni-bonn.de/~hougardy/">Home Page</a>
